{
  "id": "grammar.a2.11.02.irregulares",
  "title": "Common Irregular Pretérito Indefinido",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "Several very common verbs have irregular stems in the pretérito indefinido. Key forms include fui, hice, tuve, estuve and pude. These forms refer to completed actions just like regular forms."
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "Fui al festival.",
          "english": "I went to the festival."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Hice muchas fotografías.",
          "english": "I took many photographs."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Tuve un buen día.",
          "english": "I had a good day."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Estuve en el concierto.",
          "english": "I was at the concert."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Pude probar una comida nueva.",
          "english": "I was able to try a new food."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        [
          "fui",
          "I went / was"
        ],
        [
          "hice",
          "I did / made"
        ],
        [
          "tuve",
          "I had"
        ],
        [
          "estuve",
          "I was"
        ],
        [
          "pude",
          "I was able to"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "Use the pretérito indefinido for completed past actions. Watch the irregular forms carefully because they do not follow the regular endings."
    },
    {
      "type": "external-link",
